# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 9 as ruled: a computed answer is the next tick's input and that tick is owed, so two computing layers are two owed ticks (tick 2 fires the inner's go and shows nothing; tick 3 moves the leaf's label); a forwarding layer adds no tick and nests the path (host/[p]/0 twice over); and ch. 7 as ruled (round 3 ST): the label's move at 3 moves both hosts' `$doc`, S(3) differs from S(2), so tick 4 is owed for their publication, which nothing here reads.
